## Intelligence operator guide in Help Center and Sphinx

Context:
The User Guide buried Intelligence as Step 4 of a long workflow, the Help
Center catalog and docs hub did not list it as its own topic, and the Sphinx
toctree still pointed at satellite files that had been folded into host
guides (`features.md`, `cohort_discovery.md`, `get-started.md`). Operators
could not find Cohorts, Analytics, Communities, Patterns, Scenarios or
Compare in the published documentation.

Changes:

1. docs/intelligence.md (new)
   Operator guide for every Intelligence page: overview, prerequisites,
   Cohorts, Analytics, Communities, Patterns, when to use which, Scenarios
   (list + editor), Compare / Evaluate, run history, energy end-to-end
   example, troubleshooting. Concrete examples throughout.
2. docs/user-guide.md
   Step 4 is a map plus links to `intelligence.md`. Analytics section points
   at the operator how-to and keeps the chart/job reference.
3. src/api/routers/internal/help.py
   Catalog slug `intelligence` under Using OntoBricks (after User Guide).
4. src/front/templates/partials/layout/help_modal.html
   Resources list and workflow step 5 link to the Intelligence guide.
5. docs/README.md, docs/getting-started.md, docs/advanced_features.md,
   docs/examples.md, README.md
   Hub, next steps, advanced intro, customer-journey / family-tree examples,
   and the product README all point at `docs/intelligence.md`.
6. docs/sphinx/index.rst, docs/sphinx/guides/{intelligence,advanced-features,backend}.md,
   docs/sphinx/guides/get-started.md
   Sphinx topic toctree matches the Help Center catalog. Get Started include
   path is `getting-started.md`. Dead satellite pages stay on disk but are
   no longer in the toctree.
7. tests/units/api/test_help_api.py
   Catalog and markdown assertions for the Intelligence guide.

